== Evolution==
Evolves into '''Fujin Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Kuwagata Cat functions identically to [[Kabuto Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Kabuto Cat]], both being strong early-game units due to its stats compared to the enemies found in the Empire of Cats chapter. The only main difference is that Kuwagata trades the ability to resist [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]] with [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating Enemies]] which gives it somewhat less viability compared to Kabuto Cat. The main reason is that there are less notable floating enemies found in the Nintendo Switch version that are potent enough to give Kuwagata Cat the moment to shine as opposed to the Dark Enemies found normally throughout the game.

Kuwagata Cat ultimately struggles due to finding proper usage throughout the Nintendo Switch version and is comparably weak to its refreshed [[Kuwagata Cat (Special Cat)|mobile counterpart]] which fares much better due to improved stats across the board. The only thing going for this pathetic unit is its cheap XP costs which can improve [[User Rank]] but otherwise a useless unit as there are stronger alternatives such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)#Octopus Cat|Octopus Cat]].

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield & User Rank Dump}}

