==Trivia==
*Kuwagata Cat gets its name from ''kuwagata'', stylized antlers typically seen on [[:wikipedia:Kabuto|kabuto]] helmets. Kuwagata is also the Japanese word for "stag beetle."
*It, [[Kabuto Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Kabuto Cat]], [[Corodragon (Switch Special Cat)|Corodragon]], [[Undies Cat Jr. (Switch Special Cat)|Undies Cat Jr.]], [[Manga Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Manga Cat]], [[Manga Boogie Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Manga Boogie Cat]], and [[Manga Darabotchgogogo Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Manga Darabotchgogo Cat]] are all units that are exclusive to the Japanese version of The Battle Cats Unite!
*Kuwagata Cat's attack animation emits a wind-like element from its bite.
*Prior to [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.3 Update/WW|Patch 1.0.3]] in the International version, this was Kuwagata Cat's former description:
<pre>Cat with an awesome homemade battle helmet.
It's made of cardboard, but still pretty heavy.</pre>
<pre>Helm has been blessed by the God of Wind!
Turned deep blue after infusion of battle power!</pre>

